ecord-257rig-i2"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257rig-i2"],"id":"long.record-257rig-i2","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.108 (A restriction on dyadic rational values)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.108, p. 75, label record:257rig-i2","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*If an infinite support $A\\subseteq\\mathbb{N}_{>0}$ has $X_A(2)=p/2^c$ for integers $p$ and $c\\ge0$, then $\\sum_{a\\in A}1/a$ either diverges or converges to a value greater than $1$. The cited proof averages the shifted integer recurrence and uses a common multiple of two distinct support elements. Thus a convergent reciprocal sum of at most $1$ is excluded. This is a separate necessary condition: the reciprocal-summable criterion proved earlier already excludes every support with a convergent reciprocal sum, not just those whose sum is at most $1$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257rig-i2","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257rig-i2","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-i2%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.dyadic_support_fraction_reciprocalMass_diverges_or_gt_one%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-i2%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.dyadic_support_fraction_reciprocalMass_diverges_or_gt_one%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.dyadic_support_fraction_reciprocalMass_diverges_or_gt_one"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257rig-i2","id":"sha256:f31aeb6